  "slug": "systemin-acid-triggers-270d",
  "summary": "Recent reports link systemin perception, elicitor-triggered cell death and antiviral glycosylation to defined immune outputs in plants.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is how plants detect elicitors and convert recognition into immune outputs. In Nicotiana, four newly described bioactive systemins are detected by SlSYR1, and a premature stop codon in LAB N. benthamiana SYR1 orthologs is linked to systemin insensitivity. The secreted Ustilaginoidea virens protein UvWSC1 acts as a virulence factor and immune elicitor, triggering OsCPK13- and SOBIR1-dependent cell death. Sugarcane mosaic virus HC-Pro triggers ADR1/NRG1-dependent hypersensitive cell death in N. benthamiana, modulated by P3N-PIPO. In Arabidopsis, UGT74F1 and UGT74F2 restrict turnip mosaic virus independently of salicylic acid, jasmonate and RNA silencing. The mild SCMV maize vector is a methodological tool, and the grapevine NaBut study is applied; both are peripheral to this thread.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-25"
}
